    "note": "Complete individual Uffizi principal galleries and irregular attached ranges, long open piazzale and real flat-lintel ground colonnades with closed rear walls, three open Arno arches, middle pedimented windows, upper glazed gallery, terracotta roofs/skylights and octagonal Tribune lantern. Independent PalazzoVecchio,LoggiadeiLanzi,the river andremote VasariCorridor remain context; no interiors or copied statues. Original picture-guided relative elevations on an approximate63m standard global Terrarium reference, not a surveyed floor datum. Uniform principal floor60.6m; a bounded original north transition meets both unchanged coarse-field outer corners. Deep occupied foundations seat the Arno facade above the urban/river slope. Exact historic riverbank and threshold heights remain uncertain; no invented staircase across the Arno road, bespoke survey or wider landscape flattening. +X NNE Piazza della Signoria / open north end; -X SSW Arno loggia; +Z ESE eastern gallery; -Z WNW western gallery. +Y up. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
  },
